  "title": "Later evidence: replay counters and partial models",
  "scope": "The tree above remains the original layer 53 / forward 11 capture. These later a2 replays and component studies are separate evidence; matching token geometry does not establish the same capture, execution, cache state or timing denominator. No original Y, MFU, byte estimate or timeline interval is replaced.",
  "native_X": null,
  "original_capture_physical_MBU": null,
  "full_prefill_gain": null,
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "FC1 / FC2: six fixed serialized counter samples",
      "paragraphs": [
        "B is original N192; C selects N128 tactic (128, 1), changing both FC1 and FC2. Three pairs were collected in the fixed order B,C / C,B / B,C. Each sample has one preparation call and one profiled MoE call; FC1 and FC2 each have one NCU pass and zero profiler warmups. PDL arguments are preserved, but application replay serializes the kernel observations. Cache state and clocks were uncontrolled.",
        "Ranges below contain all three samples per arm, in bytes. They are descriptive ranges, not confidence intervals. Total-traffic differences C − B in pair order are FC1: +1,363,712, +1,304,576, +1,725,184 B; FC2: -1,087,744, -1,387,520, -492,544 B. FC1 read traffic rises while write traffic falls; its total rises in all three pairs. This does not establish a cache mechanism or explain the separate latency result.",
        "All six samples retained full finite-output and route checks; capture bit agreement is diagnostic, not paired FP64 qualification. No rate here uses a historical tree or U/S duration. A same-row profiler-duration rate describes this serialized protocol only; original concurrent HBM MBU remains unknown.",
        "A separate 90%-of-nominal compute/HBM partial scenario gives 0.583088–0.583117 ms for B and 0.582268–0.582318 ms for C. Its three paired differences are only 0.770–0.830 µs. These assumed-rate scenarios omit native instruction, synchronization, SwiGLU/scale/quantization, L2/shared/TMEM and placement/cache effects; they are not attainable native X or removable time."
      ],
      "headers": [
        "Kernel / arm",
