    {
      "title": "Indexer: a qualified carried-FFMA2 component",
      "paragraphs": [
        "The independent 147-CTA component has one or eight active warps, 168 registers and 220,160 B dynamic shared memory, with a calculated occupancy capacity of one CTA per SM; simultaneous residency was not measured. An affine full-graph completion model trains on 2,048 and 3,072 repeats and validates at 4,096. The observed slope includes loop/control and the complete component boundary; it is not native indexer arithmetic capacity.",
        "All six held-out relative errors are 0.002326%–0.008380%; all 108 measured-window clock coverage checks pass, with sampled SM/memory clocks 2,032/3,996 MHz. The component passed 79,380 full-stage and 13,230 fresh paired numerical decisions. Final observations cover the retained terminal arrays, not every internal graph invocation.",
        "Changing active warps also changes scheduler-partition coverage. The native mixed FFMA2/FADD2/merge chain, tensor/memory dependencies and Top-K are not represented by this component. No native X or gain follows; earlier collapsed-loop, scheduling and observer failures remain retained."
      ],
      "headers": [
        "Active warps per CTA",
        "Completion slope · ns/repeat",
        "Warp FFMA2 instructions/repeat"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "1",
          "51.177189–51.181477",
          "4,704"
        ],
        [
          "8",
