          "37,632"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Sparse attention: emitted schedule and scenario assumptions",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Installed 152-register and rebuilt 147-register executables remain distinct. The audited softmax core has 59/23 instruction sites before/after the prior-SV wait in the installed body, versus 74/8 in the rebuild. The old-output rescale exponential is already moved before that wait in the rebuild. Their O-rescale bodies match after the documented register renaming; this does not prove equal control encoding or isolate whole-executable timing causality.",
        "Fresh-output paired observations favored the rebuild in 23/24 unprofiled endpoint pairs and all 24 profiled kernel pairs. Both arms passed 72 paired FP64 decisions per mode and covered clock gates. Each mode failed one held-out magnitude-membership check; one unprofiled pair was adverse. Returned output/max/LSE checks on three rows do not qualify hidden QK/probability/SV pre-rounding stages, stress cases or installed-versus-ctypes API equivalence.",
        "The historical tensor-only partial is 1.050596722 ms at 100% nominal BF16 capacity, or 1.167329692 ms at an assumed 90%. Both use 2,336,462,209,024 FLOPs, 2.25 PFLOP/s, 148 SMs and a finite-placement factor 259/256 (52 SMs × 56 queries, 96 × 55). Only the assumed efficiency differs. All nonmatrix durations are omitted; neither number is a calibrated or attainable native X."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "retained_limits": [
    "No full fused-stage FP64 qualification is asserted. The separate FC1 endpoint screen covers only output[9,0].",
    "Prior N64, copy/hybrid, interleaved-M64 and failed calibration evidence remains distinct; no closed result is overwritten.",
    "No minimum-gain cutoff applies to these kernels. Prediction-validation tolerances and strict per-case max_abs AND RMSE criteria are separate requirements."
  ],
